            "content": "<p>Hormones don\u2019t operate in isolation. They respond to metabolic signals, especially how your body processes glucose and insulin.</p><p>When metabolic function is supported, the body is better able to regulate ovulation, energy, mood, and hormone signaling. When it\u2019s impaired, symptoms like irregular cycles, cravings, fatigue, and mood swings often appear, even when blood work looks \u201cnormal.\u201d</p><p>Bodology\u00ae Inositol is designed to support metabolic pathways that influence hormonal balance at the root.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "acc_line_color": "",
            "acc_text_color": "",
            "acc_title_case": "default"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_KhBe7c": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What Bodology\u00ae Inositol supports",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol helps your body respond to insulin, the silent driver behind PCOS, fertility struggles, mood shifts, and blood sugar crashes.</p><p>When taken consistently, inositol has been clinically studied to support:</p><ul><li>Healthy ovulation and cycle regularity*</li><li>Hormone balance associated with PCOS*</li><li>Insulin sensitivity and healthy blood sugar levels\u2020</li><li>Metabolic function linked to appetite regulation and weight balance\u2020  </li><li>Sleep and energy regulation*</li><li>Neurotransmitter signaling linked to mood and emotional balance*</li></ul>",
            "page": "",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "acc_line_color": "",
            "acc_text_color": "",
            "acc_title_case": "default"
          }
        },
