    "collapsible_content_cGXRUN": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_tab_hW7crK": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is inositol and how does it work?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol is a naturally occurring compound that plays a key role in insulin signaling, hormone balance, and neurotransmitter function. It's often categorized as a B-vitamin-like nutrient and has been widely researched for its role in <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/myo-inositol-impact-on-pcos-a-balancing-act\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Inositol\u2019s Impact on PCOS\u2014A Balancing Act\">PCOS</a>, <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/the-ivf-inositol-study-you-need-to-know-about\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"The IVF Inositol Study You Need to Know About\">fertility</a>, and <a href=\"https://bodology.co/blogs/bodytalks/tagged/inositol\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://bodology.co/blogs/bodytalks/tagged/inositol\">metabolic health</a>.</p><h3></h3><p></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_a3zDiF": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can you get inositol from diet alone?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol is found in foods like citrus fruit, beans, and cantaloupe\u2014but only in small amounts. You\u2019d need to eat around 8 melons a day to match the dosage in 2 scoops of Bodology. Modern farming practices have also reduced food-based inositol levels.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_KdyDNX": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is GLUT4?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>GLUT4 is a protein that helps transport glucose into cells where it can be used for energy. Inositol supports optimal GLUT4 activation, which can improve glucose metabolism.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_aTQyqe": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What makes Bodology different from other inositol supplements?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>We\u2019re a female-led, <a href=\"/pages/meet-our-experts\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Meet Our Experts\">practitioner-backed</a> brand that formulates clean, high-quality inositol based on science and real-world experience. Unlike mass brands or male-led supplement companies, we design with hormonal health, fertility, and women\u2019s lived experiences in mind. While others provide <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/which-is-better-inositol-powder-or-pills\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Which is Better: Inositol Powder Or Pills?\">capsules</a> that underdose or add ingredients like DIM or folate (which may not suit PCOS or TTC), our blend is clean, bioavailable, and practitioner-trusted.</p><p></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_ceQNA8": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does it take to see results?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Every body is different, but many users report changes in energy, cravings, mood, or cycle regularity within 4\u20138 weeks. Clinical studies show menstrual regularity and ovulation can return within 3 months in <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34624138/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34624138/\">85% of PCOS cases</a>*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_zGJYxY": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "IS THIS SAFE TO TAKE WITH PRENATALS OR GLP-1S?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Yes. Inositol is a single-ingredient supplement, not a hormone, and is generally well tolerated alongside prenatals or metabolic medications like GLP-1s. Learn more about how inositol can support your GLP-1 journey <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/glp-1-versus-inositol\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"GLP-1 vs. Inositol: Which Is Better for Weight Loss?\">here</a>. As always, confirm with your healthcare provider.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_rD7wfQ": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "ARE THERE ANY SIDE EFFECTS?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol has a strong safety record. A small number of people may experience mild bloating or digestive shifts in the first few days. Starting with 1 scoop and building up may help.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
