            "content": "<p>Inositol is found in foods like citrus fruit, beans, and cantaloupe\u2014but only in small amounts. You\u2019d need to eat around 8 melons a day to match the dosage in 2 scoops of Bodology. Modern farming practices have also reduced food-based inositol levels.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_pi8LGE": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is GLUT4?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>GLUT4 is a protein that helps transport glucose into cells where it can be used for energy. Inositol supports optimal GLUT4 activation, which can improve glucose metabolism.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_Y88xMe": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I take it?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Mix <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/is-inositol-powder-safe-and-what-dose-is-right-for-me\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Myo and D-Chiro Inositol Powder: Safety, Dose, and Everything You Need to Know\">2 scoops</a> (4g) daily into any liquid, smoothies, coffee, or water. You can even sprinkle it over food, or stir into yogurt! No pills, no binders, no bloat.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_VGwwiV": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does inositol help with PCOS?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Insulin resistance is one of the most common metabolic drivers behind PCOS, and it's what inositol works on. Inositol supports healthy insulin sensitivity \u2014 which plays a role in ovulation, hormone balance, and cycle regularity \u2014 and helps curb everyday cravings by supporting steadier blood sugar.*\u2020 The research on inositol in PCOS is strong; <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/is-inositol-powder-safe-and-what-dose-is-right-for-me\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Myo and D-Chiro Inositol Powder: Safety, Dose, and Everything You Need to Know\">see the studies here.</a> Download our<a href=\"https://bodology.co/products/metabolic-health-protocol-for-pcos\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://bodology.co/products/metabolic-health-protocol-for-pcos\"> metabolic health guide for women with PCOS</a> created in collaboration with Hillary Wright, Registered Dietitian and Author of \"The PCOS Diet Plan,\" with over 30+ years of clinical experience.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_9xTXtL": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can inositol support fertility goals?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol supports healthy ovulation and hormone balance, and has been studied in ART/IVF settings for its role in egg and embryo quality.* It's one of the most-studied nutrients in fertility research. (Research is on inositol generally, not Bodology\u00ae specifically.) Download our <a href=\"https://bodology.co/products/metabolic-health-protocol-for-fertility\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://bodology.co/products/metabolic-health-protocol-for-fertility\">metabolic health guide for fertility</a> written in collaboration with Hillary Wright, Registered Dietitian and Author of \"The PCOS Diet Plan,\" with 30+ years of clinical experience.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_Xf6BD4": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does it help with weight or cravings?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol supports <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35664247/\" title=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35664247/\">metabolic balance</a> by improving blood sugar and insulin signaling, which can influence hunger, energy, and where fat is stored. In <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30915778/\" title=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30915778/\">clinical study</a>, inositol was shown to accelerate fat loss whilst preserving lean muscle, an important factor for long term results. Improvements in hip-to-waist ratio were also seen. Learn how inositol can support your weight loss journey <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/the-ultimate-guide-to-inositol-for-weight-loss\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"The Ultimate Guide to Inositol for Weight Loss\">here</a>. Plus, download our <a href=\"https://bodology.co/products/metabolic-health-protocol-for-sustainable-weight-loss\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://bodology.co/products/metabolic-health-protocol-for-sustainable-weight-loss\">metabolic health protocol for sustainable weight loss</a>, written with Tina Kozman, CNP and Metabolic Health Expert.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_fcmKM8": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Could it influence mood, stress, or PMDD?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol participates in neurotransmitter pathways like serotonin and GABA. Some <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/is-inositol-powder-safe-and-what-dose-is-right-for-me\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Myo and D-Chiro Inositol Powder: Safety, Dose, and Everything You Need to Know\">clinical studies</a> and user experiences suggest it may support mood resilience, particularly during menstrual cycles or PMS phases. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_zqYxbN": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I take this if I don\u2019t have PCOS?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Absolutely. <a href=\"https://bodology.co/blogs/bodytalks/tagged/inositol\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://bodology.co/blogs/bodytalks/tagged/inositol\">Inositol</a> supports insulin sensitivity, energy, mood, metabolic function, and weight regulation in both PCOS and non-PCOS women.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_7Dpq3j": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I take Inositol while pregnant?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol is sometimes used during pregnancy, especially in gestational metabolic contexts. However, you should always consult your healthcare provider before starting any new supplement during pregnancy.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_NjVkTj": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is this safe to take with prenatals or GLP-1s?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Yes. Inositol is a single-ingredient supplement, not a hormone, and is generally well tolerated alongside prenatals or metabolic medications like GLP-1s. Learn more about how inositol can support your GLP-1 journey <a href=\"/blogs/bodytalks/glp-1-versus-inositol\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"GLP-1 vs. Inositol: Which Is Better for Weight Loss?\">here</a>. As always, confirm with your healthcare provider.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
